<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phărĭsaeus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φαρισαῖος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Pharisee</i>, <i>a member of the Jewish sect</i> of that name,
			usually in plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phărĭsaei</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pharīsaei</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2, 574</span></i>),
				ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φαρισαῖοι</span>, <i>the
				Pharisees</i>, a Jewish sect (eccl. Lat.),
				<i><span class="en">Tert. Praescr. 45</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Isid. 7, 6, 40</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Juvenc. 3, 221</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Marc.
				2, 16</span></i> et saep.— <i>Sing.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secundum legem Pharisaeus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Phil. 3, 5</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phărĭsaeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φαρισαῖος</span>,
				<i>Pharisœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">convivia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. 4, 66</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 5,
			20</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phărĭsăĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φαρισαικός</span>, <i>Pharisaic</i>:
			sepulcra, Hier. adv. Vigil. n. 9.</div>
